AN ACTION OF CONTRACT, TORT OR OTHERWISE, ARISING FROM, OUT OF OR IN CONNECTION
WITH THE SOFTWARE OR THE USE OR OTHER DEALINGS IN THE SOFTWARE.


2. Dictionary data and content: CC BY-SA 4.0
--------------------------------------------

The linguistic data served by the API and MCP endpoint — headwords, senses,
quotations, IPA, inflection tables, etymologies, descendants, and the Bēowulf
verse index — is derived from Wiktionary (via the kaikki.org Old English
extraction produced with wiktextract) and is licensed under the Creative Commons
Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International License (CC BY-SA 4.0):

    https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/

Under this licence you are free to share and adapt the material, provided that you:

  - Attribution — Give appropriate credit to Wiktionary and to eldertongue.com,
    link to the licence, and indicate if changes were made. Every entry page links
    to its source page on en.wiktionary.org. Please also link back to the specific
    eldertongue page you used, for example:

        https://eldertongue.com/word/cyning
        https://eldertongue.com/attribution

  - ShareAlike — If you remix, transform, or build upon the material, you must
    distribute your contributions under the same licence as the original.

  - No additional restrictions — You may not apply legal terms or technological
    measures that legally restrict others from doing anything the licence permits.

Attribution example:

    Data from eldertongue.com (https://eldertongue.com), based on Wiktionary
    contributors, licensed under CC BY-SA 4.0
    (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/).

The MIT licence above does NOT apply to the dictionary data. Code and data are
kept separate on purpose: you may reuse the code freely, but any reuse of the
linguistic content must follow CC BY-SA 4.0, including attribution and
share-alike.
